# bench/results/_cuda69/profile_prefill_1.log
#
# ARM B of the counters A/B, and the primary committed profile.
# Re-measured 2026-08-07 (Mouse, issue #69 revision) after Morpheus's tier ruling.
#
# Why this generation exists
# --------------------------
# Every earlier generation of this artifact was recorded before the trace carried a
# `vulkan.bind_check` span or a tier argument, so its span set could not answer the
# question the report now asks: how much of the Compute callback is bind checking, and
# how much is undecomposed. `--reanalyse` cannot supply that -- the spans are not in the
# stored trace -- so this is a fresh measurement, not a re-reduction.
#
# Command (from the worktree ROOT, with the release EP built from this tree):
#
#   $env:ONNXRUNTIME_VULKAN_EP_LIB               = "<worktree>/rust/target/release/onnxruntime_vulkan_ep.dll"
#   $env:ONNXRUNTIME_EP_VULKAN_BENCH_CUDA_PYTHON = "<worktree>/.venv-cu12/Scripts/python.exe"
#   # ONNXRUNTIME_EP_VULKAN_BENCH_KEEP_COUNTERS deliberately UNSET (first_run_only)
#   .venv-cu12/Scripts/python.exe -m bench.cuda_profile \
#       --workload prefill_1 --iters 10 \
#       --out bench/results/_cuda69/scratch_ab/profile_counters_off_v4.json \
#       --scratch bench/results/_cuda69/scratch_ab/off_v4
#
# The record was then copied to this name unmodified. Its `traced_record.trace_path`
# points into the gitignored scratch_ab/ directory, which holds the per-worker claim
# logs, counters dumps, ORT profiles, output tensors and the multi-MB Chrome trace this
# report reduces. That scratch is not committed; the reduction is.
#
# The tier decomposition (traced-run warm-call medians, ms)
# --------------------------------------------------------
#   tier 0  vulkan.compute_call            31.163   <- the bucketing anchor
#   tier 1    vulkan.bind_check             0.035
#   tier 1    vulkan.subgraph              31.092   <- the dispatch region
#   tier 1    unattributed_in_call          0.016
#   tier 2      record+submit+fence_wait   25.687
#   tier 2      unattributed_in_subgraph    5.187
#
# Tiers sum against their own parent and are NOT additive across tiers.
#
# The A/B result (this arm vs profile_prefill_1_counters_retained)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
#   term                        ARM B (this)   ARM A (retained)
#   unattributed_in_call_ms          0.016            36.392
#   bind_check_ms                    0.035             0.129
#   subgraph_ms                     31.092            38.259
#   compute_call_ms                 31.163            76.660
#   traced median                   31.526            78.816
#   untraced median                 30.316            71.028
#   gpu_ms_per_run                  19.002            20.179
#
# Single variable: ONNXRUNTIME_EP_VULKAN_BENCH_KEEP_COUNTERS. Same release DLL, same
# workload, same machine, same iteration counts, minutes apart.
#
# What this licenses, and what it does not
# ----------------------------------------
# It licenses: the undecomposed region inside the Compute callback is dominated by the
# harness's own counters-file dump, which lands after `dispatch_ort` returns. It moves
# 36.4 ms between arms while `bind_check` moves 0.09 ms, so the region is NOT bind-check
# time -- the claim Tank rejected, restated here as a measured refutation rather than a
# comment.
#
# It does NOT license: any ranking of remaining optimisation candidates. The two arms are
# separate processes and nothing here is subtracted across them; each row is that arm's
# own within-process number. Command/descriptor reuse is supported by the RERECORDED_
# EVERY_CALL finding but has not been ablated, so it is not ranked.
#
# ORT cross-check on this arm: ORT fused node 31.859 ms vs anchor 31.163 ms (-2.18%),
# vs inner vulkan.subgraph 31.092 ms (-2.41%). ORT's profiler shares no code with our
# tracer; it is the only independent corroboration of the anchor in this file.
#
# verdict: GPU_TIME_MEASURED, refusals: [] (required -- see
# bench/test_cuda_competition.py::test_a_committed_record_that_refuses_does_not_also_pass)
#
# The report is bench/results/_cuda69/profile_prefill_1.md; the record it was rendered
# from is bench/results/_cuda69/profile_prefill_1.json.